{"title": "ALG AVS111C-Y stereo module", "parts": {"lead": "<p class=lead>GMSL2 stereo camera module from Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech, 艾利光), with two global-shutter cameras 50 mm apart and a 6-axis IMU. One recording, solved as stereo + IMU. The recording matches ALG&#x27;s AVS111C-Y; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed by the maker.</p><div class=chips><span class=chip>Stereo</span><span class=chip>Global shutter</span><span class=chip>88 Hz IMU</span><span class=chip>GMSL2</span></div>", "glance": "<p>GMSL2 stereo camera module from Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech, 艾利光), with two global-shutter cameras 50 mm apart and a 6-axis IMU. One recording, solved as stereo + IMU. The recording matches ALG&#x27;s AVS111C-Y; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed by the maker.</p><div class=band><div class=\"demo empty\"><b>No video on this page.</b> The values below come from the solved run.</div><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.07<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>49.9<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>−4.02<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>53.9<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>No independent reference, so these values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</p>", "process": "<p>The solved path of the rig around the board. Press Play or drag the bar to follow it, and use the buttons to change the view.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"82.1,164.0 176.3,200.0 186.0,108.6 91.8,72.6 82.1,164.0\" fill=\"var(--strong)\" fill-opacity=\".1\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\"/><polyline points=\"264.6,91.7 264.8,92.1 264.6,91.9 264.5,91.7 264.8,90.5 265.0,88.9 265.6,87.9 265.6,86.6 265.5,84.9 265.4,84.6 265.3,83.9 265.5,82.6 266.2,82.3 267.4,82.1 269.6,80.8 270.8,80.