<text x=136.3 y=236 text-anchor=middle>15°</text><line class=g x1=218.7 x2=218.7 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=218.7 y=236 text-anchor=middle>30°</text><line class=g x1=301.0 x2=301.0 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=301.0 y=236 text-anchor=middle>45°</text><line class=g x1=383.3 x2=383.3 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=383.3 y=236 text-anchor=middle>60°</text><line class=g x1=465.7 x2=465.7 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=465.7 y=236 text-anchor=middle>75°</text><line class=g x1=548.0 x2=548.0 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=548.0 y=236 text-anchor=middle>90°</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=220.0 y2=220.0 /><text x=48 y=224.0 text-anchor=end>0.0</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=168.0 y2=168.0 /><text x=48 y=172.0 text-anchor=end>0.4</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=116.0 y2=116.0 /><text x=48 y=120.0 text-anchor=end>0.8</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=64.0 y2=64.0 /><text x=48 y=68.0 text-anchor=end>1.2</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=12.0 y2=12.0 /><text x=48 y=16.0 text-anchor=end>1.6</text><text x=307.0 y=254 text-anchor=middle>Ray angle from the optical axis</text><text x=12 y=110.0 text-anchor=middle transform=\"rotate(-90 12 110.0)\">Image radius / f</text><polyline class=\"c0\" points=\"54.0,220.0 70.5,213.2 86.9,206.4 103.4,199.6 119.9,192.8 136.3,185.9 152.8,179.1 169.3,172.3 185.7,165.4 202.2,158.6 218.7,151.7 235.1,144.8 251.6,137.8 268.1,130.9 284.5,123.9 301.0,116.9 317.5,109.8 333.9,102.7 350.4,95.6 366.9,88.4 383.3,81.1 399.8,73.6 416.3,65.9 432.7,57.8 449.2,49.2 465.7,39.7 482.1,29.0 498.6,16.6\"/><polyline class=\"c1\" points=\"54.0,220.0 70.5,213.2 86.9,206.4 103.4,199.6 119.9,192.8 136.3,185.9 152.8,179.1 169.3,172.3 185.7,165.4 202.2,158.5 218.7,151.6 235.1,144.7 251.6,137.8 268.1,130.8 284.5,123.8 301.0,116.7 317.5,109.7 333.9,102.6 350.4,95.6 366.9,88.6 383.3,81.7 399.8,75.0 416.3,68.6 432.7,62.8 449.2,57.6 465.7,53.4 482.1,50.5 498.6,49.5 515.1,50.9 531.5,55.6 548.0,64.5\"/></svg></div></div><p class=legend><i class=c0></i>cam0 <i class=c1></i>cam1 </p><p class=note>Read from the calibrated lens fit at the image edges, through the principal point. ~ marks an axis past the range the corners reached, where the fit is extrapolated. Past the fit means an edge lies beyond where the fit holds, so no value is given.</p>", "imu": "<div class=v data-v=\"0\"><p>Scale as deviation from 1. Model: calyx. Gyro-to-accel time offset <code>t_ga</code>: −0.71 ± 1.72 ms.</p><div class=bars><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:28.04%\"></u></i><b>+4.49 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:41.01%;width:8.99%\"></u></i><b>−1.44 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:45.12%;width:4.88%\"></u></i><b>−0.78 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:9.23%\"></u></i><b>+1.48 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:37.96%;width:12.04%\"></u></i><b>−1.93 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:5.79%\"></u></i><b>+0.93 %</b></div><div class=bar><span></span><em><s>−8 %</s><s>0</s><s>+8 %</s></em><b></b></div></div></div>", "timing": "<p>Offsets to scale, with t_imu = t_cam + td.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=chart><svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 136\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Time offsets in milliseconds, to scale\"><line class=\"g\" x1=70.0 x2=70.0 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=70.0 y=128 text-anchor=middle>-10 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=177.5 x2=177.5 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=177.5 y=128 text-anchor=middle>-5 ms</text><line class=\"g z\" x1=285.0 x2=285.0 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=285.0 y=128 text-anchor=middle>+0 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=392.5 x2=392.5 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=392.5 y=128 text-anchor=middle>+5 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=500.0 x2=500.0 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=500.0 y=128 text-anchor=middle>+10 ms</text><text x=0 y=22>cam0 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=198.6 y1=18 y2=18 /><circle class=dot cx=198.6 cy=18 r=5 /><text x=189.6 y=22 text-anchor=end>−4.02</text><text x=0 y=56>cam1 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=198.4 y1=52 y2=52 /><circle class=dot cx=198.4 cy=52 r=5 /><text x=189.4 y=56 text-anchor=end>−4.03</text><text x=0 y=90>t_ga</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=269.7 y1=86 y2=86 /><circle class=dot cx=269.7 cy=86 r=5 /><text x=260.7 y=90 text-anchor=end>−0.71</text></svg></div></div>", "results": "<p>Rotation is log(R) in rad, camera in the IMU frame.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>MVIS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>601.09</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>601.20</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>624.44</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>406.04</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>0.00856</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>0.02831</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>−0.03534</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>0.01620</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>+48.33</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+16.17</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>−17.54</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0546, −3.1331, +0.1528]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−4.018</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.580</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam1</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>598.56</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>598.49</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>624.94</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>396.48</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>0.01368</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>0.01040</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>0.00212</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>−0.00991</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>−1.54</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+17.46</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>−17.98</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0380, −3.1329, +0.1629]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−4.029</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.596</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>IMU</th></tr><tr><td>t_ga ms</td><td>−0.71 ± 1.72</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>", "limits": "<ul class=list><li>No independent reference, so these values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</li><li>A simulation of this recording, solved the same way, shows its IMU samples (about 88 Hz, unevenly spaced) can&#x27;t pin the IMU scales, the lever arm or the gyro-to-accel offset t_ga, even without noise. Treat those values as unreliable. The camera intrinsics and the stereo baseline aren&#x27;t affected.</li><li>With evenly spaced IMU samples at 150 Hz or more, the same simulation recovers most of it. The gyro scale and lever arm also need faster rotation than this recording has.</li><li>The model is matched from resolution, baseline, field of view and shutter, not confirmed by the maker.</li></ul>", "run": "<ul class=list><li>Both cameras and the IMU, global shutter, default IMU noise, t_ga on, camera intrinsics free. The IMU stored accel 4× and gyro 2× too small; both were scaled before solving. Batch of 2026-11-06.</li></ul>", "header": "<div class=sd><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><a class=sd-maker href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/\">Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech) ↗︎</a><h1 id=\"_top\">ALG AVS111C-Y stereo module</h1><p class=sd-type>GMSL2 stereo camera module with a 6-axis IMU</p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/sensors/alg-avs111c/alg-avs111c.png\" alt=\"ALG AVS111C-Y stereo camera module\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">Photo: ALG Tech, AVS111C-Y product page. Closest published model; exact model not confirmed ↗︎</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">Closest model: AVS111C-Y ↗︎</a><a class=sd-btn href=\"#specifications\">All specs (8) ↓</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>2 × 1280×800<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Shutter</dt><dd>Global<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">Maker ↗︎</a></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Field of view</dt><dd>Calibrated ~120° × 76°<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Baseline</dt><dd>49.9 mm<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>6-axis, 88 Hz here<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Output</dt><dd>GMSL2, ROS2 bag<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div></dl><p class=sd-foot>Values measured in this recording · Maker values from the AVS111C-Y product page, read 2026-11-06 · ~ is read past the range the board corners reached. Past the fit: no value, the edge lies beyond where the lens fit holds.</p></div></div></div>", "specifications": "<div class=scroll><table class=spec-table><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Published by the maker</th></tr><tr><td>Maker</td><td>Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech)</td></tr><tr><td>Closest published model</td><td>AVS111C-Y: 1280×800, 50 mm baseline, 120° × 76°, global shutter. Matched from this recording; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Lens</td><td>1.67 mm, 120° horizontal on the AVS111C-Y sheet</td></tr><tr><td>IMU</td><td>6-axis, up to 6400 Hz on the sheet; 88 Hz in this recording</td></tr><tr><td>Link and power</td><td>GMSL2, power over coax, 9 to 12 V</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Measured in these recordings</th></tr><tr><td>Cameras</td><td>2 × 1280×800, about 26 Hz in this recording</td></tr><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Global on the AVS111C-Y sheet; a rolling-shutter solve finds no readout</td></tr><tr><td>Calibrated field of view</td><td>cam0 ~120° × 76° · cam1 ~121° × 76°</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=fold id=\"sales-contact\"><summary>Sales contact <span>Provided by the maker</span></summary><div><div class=scroll><table class=spec-table><tbody><tr><td>Email</td><td><a href=\"mailto:sales@aili-light.com\">sales@aili-light.com</a></td></tr><tr><td>Phone</td><td><a href=\"tel:+8675527218150\">+86 755 2721 8150</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></details>", "rig": "<p>The solved rig in 3D, to scale. Tap a sensor for its values. Full screen lets you rotate and zoom. Grid squares are 20 mm.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><h3 class=rig-h>To scale, from above and the front</h3><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=rig-c><div class=rig-views><figure class=rig-view><figcaption>From above</figcaption><svg viewBox=\"0 0 420 262\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"From above: solved camera and IMU layout, to scale\"><line class=lever x1=\"297.8\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"114.3\" y2=\"110.5\"/><line class=lever x1=\"297.8\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"305.3\" y2=\"108.2\"/><path d=\"M114.3 110.5L45.0 70.1A80.2 80.2 0 0 1 183.6 70.2Z\" fill=\"var(--accent)\" fill-opacity=\".12\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-opacity=\".7\"/><g class=cam transform=\"translate(114.3 110.5) rotate(0.0)\"><rect x=\"-11\" y=\"-3\" width=\"22\" height=\"9\" rx=\"2.5\" fill=\"var(--accent)\"/><rect x=\"-4.5\" y=\"-6\" width=\"9\" height=\"4\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"var(--accent)\"/></g><path d=\"M305.3 108.2L235.6 68.5A80.2 80.2 0 0 1 375.0 68.5Z\" fill=\"var(--ghost)\" fill-opacity=\".12\" stroke=\"var(--ghost)\" stroke-opacity=\".7\"/><g class=cam transform=\"translate(305.3 108.2) rotate(-0.0)\"><rect x=\"-11\" y=\"-3\" width=\"22\" height=\"9\" rx